{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeskHPpVFACdSP8QPCMKt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me look at the complete directory structure and then move to the DESIGN phase.\n\n## ANALYSIS SUMMARY\n\n**Requirement, restated:**\nAdd a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that moves a shipment from CREATED to CONFIRMED status, is idempotent (CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED succeeds silently), returns 409 for CANCELLED shipments, and 404 for non-existent shipments.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27` — status enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- Repository: `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-22` — has save(), findById(), existsById()\n- Controller: `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — current endpoints: POST (create), GET /{id}, GET (list)\n- Exception handling: `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- Error codes: `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum used in exceptions\n- Exception mapping: `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` — converts ApiException to ApiError response\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n1. Exceptions: ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409; both extend ApiException\n2. Error codes: Defined centrally in ErrorCode enum; each exception carries a code\n3. Controllers: @RestController, @RequestMapping base path, @PostMapping/@GetMapping for actions\n4. Response shape: ResponseEntity<T> for successful POST; body only for GET\n5. Status codes: 201 CREATED for POST create, 200 OK for GET and other POST actions\n6. Repository methods: save(entity), findById(id), existsById(id)\n7. Tests: @SpringBootTest, @AutoConfigureMockMvc, MockMvc for HTTP assertions\n\n**Affected files — must change:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Add ErrorCode for \"shipment already cancelled\"\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add 4 tests (confirm CREATED, confirm CONFIRMED, confirm CANCELLED, confirm not found)\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Idempotency correctness — must not error on CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED\n2. Immutable Shipment — must create new instance with updated status\n3. Test isolation — must not break existing tests\n\n**Open questions:** None; the ticket is fully specified.\n\n---\n\n## DESIGN\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED` to ErrorCode enum (line 36, before VALIDATION_FAILED)\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add new method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` after `getById`:\n   - Route: `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`\n   - Logic: \n     - If shipment not found → throw ResourceNotFoundException\n     - If shipment status is CANCELLED → throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED)\n     - If shipment status is CREATED → save with status=CONFIRMED, return updated shipment\n     - If shipment status is CONFIRMED → do nothing, return existing shipment\n   - Return: ResponseEntity.ok(shipment)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add 4 test methods:\n   - `confirms a shipment in CREATED status` — creates S-confirm-1, confirms it, expects 200 with CONFIRMED status\n   - `confirming an already-confirmed shipment succeeds` — creates S-confirm-2, confirms twice, expects both to succeed with 200\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409` — manually inserts CANCELLED shipment to repo, tries to confirm, expects 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404` — tries to confirm non-existent, expects 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Adding a `Service` layer between controller and repository: Rejected because existing endpoints (create, getById, list) do not use one; consistency with existing architecture takes precedence over separation of concerns for a single state transition.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Case 1: CREATED → CONFIRMED*\n- Read: repository.findById(shipmentId) → returns Shipment(status=CREATED)\n- Write: repository.save(Shipment(..., status=CONFIRMED))\n- Return: ResponseEntity.ok(Shipment(..., status=CONFIRMED)), HTTP 200\n\n*Case 2: CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED (idempotent)*\n- Read: repository.findById(shipmentId) → returns Shipment(status=CONFIRMED)\n- Write: None (status already correct)\n- Return: ResponseEntity.ok(Shipment(..., status=CONFIRMED)), HTTP 200\n\n*Case 3: CANCELLED → attempt confirm*\n- Read: repository.findById(shipmentId) → returns Shipment(status=CANCELLED)\n- Write: None\n- Throw: ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED, message)\n- Return: GlobalExceptionHandler maps to ApiError with code, HTTP 409\n\n*Case 4: Non-existent shipment*\n- Read: repository.findById(shipmentId) → returns null\n- Write: None\n- Throw: ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message)\n- Return: GlobalExceptionHandler maps to ApiError with code, HTTP 404\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED) verifies status changes\n- Test 2: Idempotency (CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED) verifies no-op on second call\n- Test 3: Conflict (CANCELLED) verifies error code and HTTP 409\n- Test 4: Not found verifies error code and HTTP 404\n\n---\n\nNow I'll implement the changes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1387,"cache_read_input_tokens":17519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1387},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d46de782-f925-4b08-8c72-ef7ff90d09db","uuid":"46fe033c-dc3f-4d22-833c-7a59e688a039","timestamp":"2026-09-09T10:58:39.642Z","request_id":"req_011CeskHNzNw7WEcTMyuYRdY"}
