ate (Kotlin idiom)\n   - Follows existing exception patterns (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException)\n   - No changes to existing methods or imports\n   - No unrelated refactoring\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 4 test methods (lines 85-129):\n   - Each test covers one requirement case\n   - Uses existing MockMvc patterns\n   - Uses existing `createShipment()` helper and repository access\n   - Tests follow naming convention: backtick-quoted descriptive names\n   - No changes to existing tests\n\n**No unresolved findings** — All ticket requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n---\n\n## DONE\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint that transitions CREATED→CONFIRMED (idempotent), rejects CANCELLED with 409, and not-found with 404\n\nChanged       ApiError.kt — added SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED error code for the conflict case\n              ShipmentController.kt — added confirm() endpoint with state validation and idempotent behavior\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added 4 tests covering CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotency, CANCELLED rejection, and 404\n\nTests         Test 1: \"confirms a shipment in CREATED status\" — verifies CREATED→CONFIRMED transition and persistence\n              Test 2: \"confirming an already-confirmed shipment succeeds\" — verifies idempotency (CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED no-op)\n              Test 3: \"rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409\" — verifies CANCELLED→* throws ConflictException\n              Test 4: \"rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404\" — verifies missing shipment throws ResourceNotFoundException\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test (from sample-service/)\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS; Tests run: 17, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\n\nNot done      (none - all requirements implemented and verified)\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_to